 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb150596",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Pairs Trading: Coca-Cola (KO) vs PepsiCo (PEP)\n",
    "\n",
    "Steps:\n",
    "1. Download prices with `yfinance`\n",
    "2. Check **correlation** (returns) and look at the scatter plot\n",
    "3. Test for **cointegration** (Engle-Granger)\n",
    "4. Build the **spread** and its **z-score**\n",
    "5. Estimate mean-reversion **half-life**\n",
    "6. Run a simple **backtest** (hedge ratio fit on train data only, traded on test data)\n",
    "\n",
    "*Educational only, not financial advice.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "798e8fc1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# !pip install yfinance statsmodels pandas numpy matplotlib"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "189f4e70",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import yfinance as yf\n",
    "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
    "from statsmodels.tsa.stattools import coint, adfuller\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (11, 5)\n",
    "plt.rcParams['axes.grid'] = True"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "39a58163",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Download data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fb823a86",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "A, B = 'KO', 'PEP'\n",
    "START, END = '2015-01-01', '2025-12-31'\n",
    "\n",
    "raw = yf.download([A, B], start=START, end=END, auto_adjust=True, progress=False)\n",
    "prices = raw['Close'].dropna()\n",
    "prices = prices[[A, B]]\n",
    "print(prices.shape)\n",
    "prices.tail()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "46e032dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Rebased to 100 so both lines start at the same point\n",
    "(prices / prices.iloc[0] * 100).plot(title=f'{A} vs {B} (rebased to 100)')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "18413848",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Correlation (use returns, not prices)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a2495fa5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "returns = prices.pct_change().dropna()\n",
    "corr = returns[A].corr(returns[B])\n",
    "print(f'Correlation of daily returns {A} vs {B}: {corr:.3f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax = returns.plot.scatter(x=A, y=B, alpha=0.3, title=f'Daily returns scatter (corr = {corr:.2f})')\n",
    "ax.axhline(0, color='k', lw=0.5); ax.axvline(0, color='k', lw=0.5)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "53f7c64f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Correlation is not stable over time\n",
    "returns[A].rolling(90).corr(returns[B]).plot(title='Rolling 90-day correlation')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a997aa14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Cointegration test (Engle-Granger)\n",
    "\n",
    "Correlation says returns move together day to day. Cointegration asks whether the **price spread** keeps returning to a stable level. A small p-value (< 0.05) is evidence of cointegration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "83ca23fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "log_prices = np.log(prices)\n",
    "\n",
    "score, pvalue, _ = coint(log_prices[A], log_prices[B])\n",
    "print(f'Engle-Granger t-stat: {score:.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'p-value: {pvalue:.4f}')\n",
    "print('Cointegrated at 5%' if pvalue < 0.05 else 'No evidence of cointegration at 5%')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c3e6010c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Train / test split and hedge ratio\n",
    "\n",
    "The hedge ratio (beta) is estimated on the **first 60%** of data only. Estimating on all data would leak future information into the backtest."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "45102ff1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "split = int(len(log_prices) * 0.6)\n",
    "train, test = log_prices.iloc[:split], log_prices.iloc[split:]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Regress log(A) on log(B): log(A) = alpha + beta * log(B) + error\n",
    "X = sm.add_constant(train[B])\n",
    "ols = sm.OLS(train[A], X).fit()\n",
    "alpha, beta = ols.params['const'], ols.params[B]\n",
    "print(f'alpha = {alpha:.4f}, hedge ratio beta = {beta:.4f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Spread = log(A) - beta * log(B)\n",
    "spread = log_prices[A] - beta * log_prices[B]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Does the train spread look stationary?\n",
    "adf_p = adfuller(spread.iloc[:split])[1]\n",
    "print(f'ADF p-value of train spread: {adf_p:.4f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "spread.plot(title='Spread (log KO - beta * log PEP)')\n",
    "plt.axvline(prices.index[split], color='red', ls='--', label='train | test')\n",
    "plt.axhline(spread.iloc[:split].mean(), color='k', lw=0.8)\n",
    "plt.legend(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b31ad70d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Half-life of mean reversion\n",
    "\n",
    "Fit `Δspread_t = λ · spread_{t-1} + ε`. Half-life = `-ln(2) / λ` days. It tells you roughly how long a deviation takes to close halfway."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "59c94ca4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "s_train = spread.iloc[:split]\n",
    "lag = s_train.shift(1).dropna()\n",
    "delta = s_train.diff().dropna()\n",
    "lam = sm.OLS(delta, sm.add_constant(lag)).fit().params.iloc[1]\n",
    "\n",
    "half_life = -np.log(2) / lam if lam < 0 else np.inf\n",
    "print(f'lambda = {lam:.4f}, half-life = {half_life:.1f} trading days')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c0dc0694",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Z-score and trading signals\n",
    "\n",
    "- z-score = (spread − rolling mean) / rolling std\n",
    "- **z > entry**: spread too high → short A, long B\n",
    "- **z < −entry**: spread too low → long A, short B\n",
    "- Exit when z returns near 0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fe85fb91",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "WINDOW = 60       # rolling window for mean/std\n",
    "ENTRY  = 2.0\n",
    "EXIT   = 0.5\n",
    "COST   = 0.0005   # 5 bps per unit of position change (rough transaction cost)\n",
    "\n",
    "roll_mean = spread.rolling(WINDOW).mean()\n",
    "roll_std  = spread.rolling(WINDOW).std()\n",
    "z = (spread - roll_mean) / roll_std\n",
    "\n",
    "z_test = z.iloc[split:].dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "pos, positions = 0, []\n",
    "for val in z_test:\n",
    "    if pos == 0:\n",
    "        if val > ENTRY:   pos = -1   # short the spread\n",
    "        elif val < -ENTRY: pos = 1   # long the spread\n",
    "    elif pos == 1 and val >= -EXIT:\n",
    "        pos = 0\n",
    "    elif pos == -1 and val <= EXIT:\n",
    "        pos = 0\n",
    "    positions.append(pos)\n",
    "\n",
    "positions = pd.Series(positions, index=z_test.index, name='position')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(11, 7), sharex=True)\n",
    "z_test.plot(ax=axes[0], title='Z-score (test period)')\n",
    "for lvl in (ENTRY, -ENTRY): axes[0].axhline(lvl, color='red', ls='--')\n",
    "for lvl in (EXIT, -EXIT):   axes[0].axhline(lvl, color='green', ls=':')\n",
    "positions.plot(ax=axes[1], drawstyle='steps-post', title='Position (+1 long spread, -1 short spread)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "edaeb6ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Backtest\n",
    "\n",
    "Position is **lagged one day** (signal today, trade tomorrow) to avoid look-ahead bias. Daily P&L ≈ position × change in the log-spread, minus costs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e19c05a8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "spread_test = spread.loc[positions.index]\n",
    "pnl_gross = positions.shift(1) * spread_test.diff()\n",
    "trades = positions.diff().abs().fillna(0)\n",
    "pnl_net = pnl_gross - trades * COST * (1 + abs(beta))   # both legs cost money\n",
    "pnl_net = pnl_net.dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "equity = pnl_net.cumsum()\n",
    "\n",
    "def sharpe(x):\n",
    "    return np.sqrt(252) * x.mean() / x.std() if x.std() > 0 else np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Number of position changes: {int(trades.sum())}')\n",
    "print(f'Total return (log, approx.): {equity.iloc[-1]:.2%}')\n",
    "print(f'Annualised Sharpe:           {sharpe(pnl_net):.2f}')\n",
    "print(f'Max drawdown:                {(equity - equity.cummax()).min():.2%}')\n",
    "\n",
    "equity.plot(title='Cumulative P&L of the pairs strategy (test period)')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "11e58cb5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Things to try next\n",
    "\n",
    "- Tune `ENTRY`, `EXIT`, `WINDOW` (beware of overfitting to the test period)\n",
    "- Re-estimate the hedge ratio on a rolling basis (or use a Kalman filter)\n",
    "- Try other pairs: V/MA, XOM/CVX, HDFCBANK.NS / ICICIBANK.NS\n",
    "- Add a stop-loss: relationships can break permanently\n",
    "- Check whether cointegration holds in the test period too"
   ]
  },
